WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.120
Let's understand another example on a new page.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.100
Assume you have three red marbles and three blue marbles in a box.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.640
Your task is to pull out two marbles out of these six marbles,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.540
one after the other.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.020
This example is interesting, but I need you to focus really really hard.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.240
So there will be two cases here!

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.600
First case, you pick the first marble out and then put it back

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.820
and then take the second marble out.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.860
You take one out, put it back in and then pick the second marble.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.580
Let's talk about this case first.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.740
Say we want to find the probability of getting a red marble

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.940
out in your first chance.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.280
Let's call it P of R1.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.180
There are three red marbles and six marbles in all.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.620
So the probability of getting a red marble is 'three by six'.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.060
The numerator tells us that we can pick a red marble in three ways

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.660
and the denominator tells us the total number of marbles.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.960
So you picked one red marble up and placed it back in.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.740
Now what is the probability of picking a red marble in your second chance?

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.900
We call it P of R2.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.240
Since we place the ball back in

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.760
there are three red marbles and six total marbles.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.500
So the probability still remains 'three by six', it's unchanged.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.400
So these two events are called independent events.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.520
The probability does not change if the marble is replaced.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.580
It's because we have the same set of marbles we had originally.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.620
Now let's look at the second case.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.520
You pick one marble out and then pick the second one out

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.500
without putting it back in.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.260
Now it gets even more interesting.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.200
Focus hard.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.920
In this case we pick one marble,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.320
we do not put it back in and then we pick a second marble.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.900
Now let's find the probability of picking a red marble in your first chance.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.160
It will be 'three by six'.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.940
You can pick a red marble in three ways out of the six possible marbles.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.780
So assume the red marble is taken out.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.480
But remember, this time it's not put back in the box.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.980
It remains outside.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.260
Now what is the probability of picking a red marble?

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.720
There are two red marbles and five in total.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:31.720
So the probability of picking a red marble is 'two by five'.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.120
Did you observe what happened?

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.340
We can see that the probability has changed if the marble is not replaced.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.580
So in this case, the events are not independent.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.980
Now forget the colour of the marbles.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.840
You should know that if a marble is put back in,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.760
then the events will be independent

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.780
as the sample space does not change for the second case.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.520
But if the marble is not put back in,

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.620
then the sample space changes for the second event

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.580
which is why the events are not independent.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.320
The probability of second event actually depends on

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.660
what marble you have picked first.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.580
We will understand what mutually exclusive means in our next video.

